    "2": {
      "contract": "Uniform ABI and standard/cached behavior",
      "trace": "Reflection records a uniform member name, byte offset and size but not scalar kind or vector/matrix shape. Cached write_uniform selects bytes from the supplied PassParameter variant without comparing member size or type; a supplied u32 value1 for a hypothetical f32 member writes integer bits rather than f32 1.0 bits. For a hypothetical reflected scalar at byte12 of a16-byte block, a supplied Vec2 would exceed the block and its put closure silently skips the write before returning Ok. Fast mode reports an omitted member, while the selected general ComputePass source initializes the block to zeros and does nothing for omitted members or unsupported variants.",
      "remaining": "Original Adler356 queue151 already requires tracing standard packing and no silent out-of-block write; delegate740 separately recorded distinct fast error-reason contracts. No shader, reflection, bytes, cast, output, pass or test ran. Actual valid WGSL layouts, all parameter producers, standard path policies and exact related aliases remain open."
